arithmetic -- drill in sums===========================    arithmetic -o +-x/ -r 12It asks twenty problems at a time and keeps asking each until the answeris right, answering `What?' to a wrong one; after every twenty it printsthe rights, wrongs, score and the seconds per problem.  Numbers it gotwrong come round again more often, and the bias fades as you get themright.`-o' picks the operations from + - x /, addition and subtraction bydefault; `-r' is the largest operand, 10 by default.  ^C or end of inputstops it and prints the score so far.By Eamonn McManus, Trinity College Dublin, as 4.3BSD Net/2 carried it,from The Unix Heritage Society's archive.  Full originals inSRC/arithmetic/ORIG.